# string_matching:
# CSES 1753, String Matching (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1753), in our own words:
# a text and a pattern, strings over the lowercase letters; the number of places of
# the text where the pattern occurs, a place counting when the pattern's letters are
# the text's from there on. The input is the text and then the pattern, each a Scott
# list (corpora/library/prelude/list) of binary naturals
# (corpora/library/binary/natural), a = 0 to z = 25, the pattern nonempty, and the
# answer a binary natural. Part of the CSES port's fourth batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: at each place of the text, the pattern is
# compared with the text from there letter by letter, and fails at the first letter
# that differs or at the end of the text; the places where the whole pattern matched
# are counted. Its reading compares about n times m letters; the replacement the
# family asks for is the Z-function or the Knuth-Morris-Pratt prefix function, which
# never compares a letter of the text twice, in about n + m steps, on fixed-width
# integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application only:
# its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal. It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion consumes the finite text
# (the places) or the finite pattern; the branches that a Scott boolean discards are
# never read. The program calls no subtraction. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the
# soundness of the derivable equations for the contextual preorder of Definition 14
# (Lean `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W, while
# Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to λx y. y, and
# applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ true false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero _ _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ merge_binary_equality
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self pattern text
    . pattern true
      λ wanted wanted_rest
      . text false λ letter rest. merge_binary_equality wanted letter (self wanted_rest rest) false
  )
λ starts_with
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ pattern
    . fixpoint
      ( λ self text found
        . ( λ found_here. text found_here λ _ rest. self rest found_here )
          (starts_with pattern text (merge_binary_increment found) found)
      )
  )
λ occurrences
. (λtuple. tuple λtext pattern. occurrences pattern text binary_zero)
λ string_matching
. export string_matching
